NPZSee 0.1.0
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later

npzsee is an independently named Rust rewrite derived from and inspired by
npyquick. It is a continuation of that project's array-viewing concepts and
behavior, rather than a claim that all design and provenance are unrelated.

Upstream: https://github.com/LiukDiihMieu/npyquick
Upstream base commit: 6be16fd (2026 source snapshot).
Upstream copyright: Copyright (C) 2026 LiukDiihMieu.
Rust rewrite and modifications: Copyright (C) 2026 npzsee contributors.

Modifications include native Rust data loading and rendering, background jobs,
array sidebar, table-first hierarchy and JSON navigation, histogram area fill,
six-language localization, docked cell inspection, native/pip packaging,
portability fixes, and a separate name. See CHANGELOG.md and agent.md.

